{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftAFNrALLcLM7cmWagZc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sitting 001 is recorded, but no rows could be re-anchored. Every one of the three registries still holds a row I sent back, and the snapshot copy refuses while those rows drift.\n\n**Verdict** (`11b05f31`, trailer `WI: WI-880`, file `docs/reviews/wi-880/001-ADJUDICATE-9a39f47.md`, ending `SITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment;first-approval`)\n\n**Amendment: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=9`.** Every row adds an obligation.\n\n- **Blessed (5): SR-019, SR-020, LLR-021, TC-021, SR-046.** The single interpreter probe `kit-python.sh` and all three hooks match LLR-021 exactly. One note on SR-019: its new clause says \"the commit hooks\", which also covers commit-msg, although the row names only pre-commit. The code meets it, so I didn't send it back.\n- **Not blessed (4):**\n  - **SR-032:** SR-032 is about the shipped dev-setup templates. The new Windows install clause describes behaviour only this repo's own `scripts/dev-setup.ps1` has. The shipped `dev-setup.template.ps1` offers only an adopter-configured install command, empty by default. It neither looks for uv or winget nor searches again afterwards.\n  - **TC-345:** it now checks three things no requirement row states:\n    - this repo's committed settings carry no guard group;\n    - the inert example's contents;\n    - the readiness report names whether the hooks opt-in is on.\n  - **LLR-047 and TC-047:** LLR-047 claims a run-menu line's bare `python3` runs on the menu's interpreter on Windows, and it doesn't. A Windows interpreter folder has no `python3.exe`. I reproduced it: with PATH reduced to System32, `python3` is \"not recognized\". With the full PATH it reaches the WindowsApps alias instead. TC-047 never drives `python3` on Windows, which is how this got through.\n\n**First approval: `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=2`** (LLR-326 and TC-350). The approved SR-032 doesn't call for LLR-326; only the amended clause I returned does. TC-350 also says both the decline and accept paths search again, while LLR-326 says only after acceptance. I changed no Status cells and took no approval snapshot.\n\n**Re-attestation act:** `intake.py snapshot --reattests SR-019,SR-020,SR-046,LLR-021,TC-021` was refused, naming SR-032, LLR-047, TC-345 and TC-047. Nothing was written, and the working tree is clean. The five blessed rows stay unanchored until the lane answers the findings. Put them in the same sitting as the corrected rows.\n\n**Decision for you:** the follow-up drafts are in the verdict file, but nothing will act on them automatically. WI-880 is an ordinary work spec, and intake only mints `## Dispositions` drafts from adjudication specs, so I wrote them under the amendment heading rather than in the spec. There are three, and you would need to route them back to the WI-880 lane or file them:\n\n1. Give SR-032's Windows install clause, with LLR-326 and TC-350, a home that names this repo's own dev-setup. Or make the shipped templates find a provisioner and search again.\n2. State TC-345's three this-repo checks in LLR-322 or a proper parent row.\n3. Make bare `python3` run the menu's interpreter on Windows, or narrow the claim, and extend TC-047 to test it.\n\n**Tests:** the arms-map tests ran 21 passed, 1 skipped. The skip is the POSIX-only case, because this box is Windows."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":812,"cache_read_input_tokens":180866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":812},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a511e73-e906-4589-9f31-ae73f8534ed7","uuid":"d91dad37-eb62-427b-bfaf-62efe524458d","timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:27:12.155Z","request_id":"r